<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers Argentine farmers had harvested 85.4 percent of their 1996/97 maize crop by May 23, the Agriculture Secretariat said in weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared with only 76.8 percent progress by the same date the previous season. Soybean harvesting was 92.3 percent complete, compared with 73.8 percent progress by the same date in 1996. Cotton harvesting was 66.7 percent complete, compared with 53.7 percent progress at the same stage last season. Good rains fell throughout most grains areas. But some areas in Cordoba, Santa Fe and La Pampa still need more water.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,926  100.0(100.0) 2,793.5   85.4  (76.8)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 5,914.0   92.3  (73.8)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,934.1   99.9  (100.0</p>
<p> Sorghum     784  100.0(100.0)   597.3   83.6  (73.6)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   589.1   66.7  (53.7)</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
